---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Intents
description: The intent vocabulary, and the components and patterns that declare each intent.
---
<section class="docs-page-intro">
  <div class="docs-eyebrow">
    <aihio-badge variant="outline">{{ docs.intentCount }} intents</aihio-badge>
  </div>
  <h1>Intents</h1>
  <p>
    An intent names what a piece of UI is for: <code>primary-action</code>, <code>selection</code>,
    <code>modal</code>. Every component and pattern declares the intents it serves, so a request can be matched to a
    component by meaning before anything is said about how it looks. This is the map an agent reads from the prompt
    fragment and the MCP server's <code>find</code> tool, as a page.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="docs-section-heading">
    <div>
      <h2>From intent to component</h2>
      <p>
        Mark up an element with <code>data-aihio-intent</code> to say which one it serves. The linter checks the
        annotation against the component's schema, so a claim it cannot back is an error.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <dl class="docs-intents">
    {% for intent in docs.intents %}
      <div class="docs-intents__row" id="{{ intent.name }}">
        <dt><code>{{ intent.name }}</code></dt>
        <dd class="docs-intents__meaning">{{ intent.description | prose | safe }}</dd>
        <dd class="docs-intents__used">
          {% if intent.components.length %}
            <ul class="docs-intents__links" aria-label="Components">
              {% for component in intent.components %}
                <li><a class="docs-inline-link" href="{{ component.path | docsUrl(page.url) }}">{{ component.name }}</a></li>
              {% endfor %}
            </ul>
          {% else %}
            <span class="docs-muted">No component of its own: compose it.</span>
          {% endif %}
          {% if intent.patterns.length %}
            <ul class="docs-intents__links docs-intents__links--patterns" aria-label="Patterns">
              {% for pattern in intent.patterns %}
                <li><a class="docs-inline-link" href="{{ pattern.path | docsUrl(page.url) }}">{{ pattern.name }}</a></li>
              {% endfor %}
            </ul>
          {% endif %}
        </dd>
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </dl>
</section>
